<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Immortal</h1>
<p>The immortals, or admins, are the people who run Valhalla: players who 
have played for a long time and now build, program and look after the 
game. Their level is 200 or more, and they can't die.
</p><p>What they can do grows with their level. Some only watch the game. Game 
masters stage events and quests in the world. Moderators deal with players 
who disrupt the game for others, and the highest look after players' 
characters and run the game itself.
</p><p>Immortals are usually busy testing something or helping someone, so don't 
pester them; but if you need help, a polite tell is fine. They may not 
help mortals along: no handing out experience, gold or equipment, and an 
immortal who does can be removed.
</p><p>To reach the admins about a problem, use <a cmd='#'>bug</a> for something broken, 
<a cmd='#'>typo</a> for a spelling mistake and <a cmd='#'>idea</a> for a suggestion.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
